{"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule","doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/OrientedIncidenceMatrix"]]},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/OrientedIncidenceMatrix\/init(_:)-y850","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"metadata":{"remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/OrientedIncidenceMatrix.swift#L154","fileName":"OrientedIncidenceMatrix.swift"},"roleHeading":"Initializer","modules":[{"name":"IncidenceMatrixModule"}],"title":"init(_:)","fragments":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"init"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"H"},{"kind":"text","text":">("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"H"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"role":"symbol","extendedModule":"IncidenceMatrixModule","symbolKind":"init","externalID":"s:21IncidenceMatrixModule08OrientedaB0VyACxc14GraphProtocols08DirectedE0RzAD0G10HypergraphRzlufc"},"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"init"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"H"},{"kind":"text","text":">("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"_"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"internalParam","text":"hypergraph"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"H"},{"kind":"text","text":") "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"where"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"H"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P","text":"DirectedGraph"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"H"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedHypergraph","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols18DirectedHypergraphP","text":"DirectedHypergraph"}]}],"kind":"declarations"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/incidencematrixmodule\/orientedincidencematrix\/init(_:)-y850"]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The one hypergraph conversion for a type that is both a directed graph and a directed"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"hypergraph: read as a hypergraph."}],"references":{"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/DirectedGraph":{"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"DirectedGraph","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","title":"DirectedGraph","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"DirectedGraph","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/directedgraph","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A directed graph: a finite set of vertices and a finite collection of directed edges between"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"them."}],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph"},"doc://IncidenceMatrixModule/documentation/IncidenceMatrixModule/OrientedIncidenceMatrix":{"url":"\/documentation\/incidencematrixmodule\/orientedincidencematrix","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The oriented incidence matrix of a directed hypergraph: entry (v, p) is −1 when "},{"code":"v","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is a source"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of column "},{"code":"p","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", +1 when it is a target, and 0 otherwise. Gallo, Longo, Pallottino and Nguyen"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(1993) define a directed hypergraph’s matrix this way (aᵢⱼ = −1 for a tail node, 1 for a head"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"node); a directed graph’s edge is the column with one source and one target, the matrix of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"spectral graph theory (B·Bᵀ = L, Godsil–Royle §8.3) and NetworkX’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"incidence_matrix(oriented=True)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". It conforms to "},{"code":"DirectedHypergraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", so the "},{"code":"Hypergraphs","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"algorithms (B- and F-connection, components, the clique expansion) run on it unchanged; it is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"not a "},{"code":"DirectedGraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"title":"OrientedIncidenceMatrix","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"OrientedIncidenceMatrix"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/OrientedIncidenceMatrix","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"OrientedIncidenceMatrix"}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/DirectedHypergraph":{"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"DirectedHypergraph","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","title":"DirectedHypergraph","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"DirectedHypergraph","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/directedhypergraph","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A directed hypergraph: a finite set of vertices and a finite collection of hyperedges, each an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"ordered pair of vertex sets, its sources (tail) and its targets (head). Gallo, Longo, Pallottino"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and Nguyen, “Directed hypergraphs and applications”, "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Discrete Applied Mathematics"}]},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"42(2–3):177–201, 1993, define a hyperarc as “an ordered pair … of (possibly empty) disjoint"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"subsets”; here either side may be empty and a vertex may be on both, the hypergraph form of a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"self-loop (XGI’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DiHypergraph"},{"type":"text","text":" allows both)."}],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedHypergraph"},"doc://IncidenceMatrixModule/documentation/IncidenceMatrixModule/OrientedIncidenceMatrix/init(_:)-y850":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The one hypergraph conversion for a type that is both a directed graph and a directed"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"hypergraph: read as a hypergraph."}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","title":"init(_:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/OrientedIncidenceMatrix\/init(_:)-y850","url":"\/documentation\/incidencematrixmodule\/orientedincidencematrix\/init(_:)-y850","fragments":[{"text":"init","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"H","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"text":"H","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}]},"doc://IncidenceMatrixModule/documentation/IncidenceMatrixModule":{"url":"\/documentation\/incidencematrixmodule","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","abstract":[],"title":"IncidenceMatrixModule"}}}